skill: API Testing

@ API Testing Basics | B
What does API testing primarily validate?
= The business logic, data and responses at the service layer without using the UI
- Only the colors of the web page
- Only the database indexes
- Only the browser compatibility
? API tests send requests directly to endpoints and check the responses.

@ API Testing Basics | B
Which tool is widely used for manual API testing?
= Postman
- Photoshop
- Notepad only
- Figma
? Postman lets you build requests, send them and inspect responses.

@ API Testing Basics | I
Besides the response body, what else should an API test normally check?
= The status code and the headers
- The window size of the browser
- The color of the response
- The font of the documentation
? A complete test verifies status, headers, body and sometimes response time.

@ Status Codes and Validation | I
A GET request for /users/999 where no such user exists should usually return:
= 404
- 200
- 201
- 500
? 404 Not Found tells the client that the resource does not exist.

@ Status Codes and Validation | I
What does a 400 Bad Request response indicate?
= The client sent a malformed or invalid request
- The server crashed
- The resource was created
- The user is not logged in
? A 4xx code means the problem is with the request.

@ Status Codes and Validation | I
What does a 500 status code indicate?
= An internal server error
- A successful response
- A redirect
- A missing resource
? 5xx codes indicate that the server failed to handle a valid request.

@ Status Codes and Validation | A
Which is a good negative test for POST /users when email is a required field?
= Send a body without email and expect 400 with a clear error message
- Send a valid body and expect 201
- Send the same valid body twice and ignore the result
- Call GET /users
? Negative tests confirm that the API rejects invalid input properly.

@ Status Codes and Validation | A
What is schema validation in API testing?
= Verifying that the response structure and data types match the agreed contract
- Checking the file size of the response
- Validating the HTML of a web page
- Counting the number of requests
? Schema checks catch missing fields or wrong types that value checks might miss.

@ Postman | I
What is a Postman collection?
= A group of saved requests that can be organized and run together
- A list of browsers
- A database backup
- A type of API key
? Collections can be shared and run with the collection runner.

@ Postman | I
Which Postman feature lets you write JavaScript assertions on the response?
= The Tests tab
- The Console only
- The Params tab
- The Authorization tab
? The Tests tab runs scripts after the response arrives, for example pm.test checks.

@ Postman | I
What are environments and variables in Postman used for?
= Reusing values such as base URL or tokens across requests and environments
- Changing the color theme
- Compressing responses
- Writing documentation only
? Variables avoid hard-coded values and make it easy to switch between dev, test and production.

@ Authentication and Security | A
Which header typically carries a bearer token?
= Authorization
- Content-Length
- Accept-Language
- User-Agent
? The format is Authorization: Bearer followed by the token.

@ Authentication and Security | A
Which test verifies authorization on a restricted endpoint?
= Calling it as a user without the required role and expecting 403
- Calling it with a valid admin token and expecting 200 only
- Calling it with a very long URL
- Calling it with an empty body
? Authorization tests confirm that users cannot access resources they are not permitted to use.

@ Authentication and Security | I
A request is sent without any token to a protected endpoint. What should the API return?
= 401 Unauthorized
- 200 OK
- 201 Created
- 204 No Content
? Missing credentials should be rejected with 401.
